About the 3rd point: all the methods in the SDK are tested, so there is no unexpected slash generation. The only way for the user to add an unexpected slash is during the client declaration:

```php
$client = new MeiliSearch\Client('http://127.0.0.1:7700/');
// instead of
$client = new MeiliSearch\Client('http://127.0.0.1:7700');
```

It will not work because MeiliSearch API does not handle the double slashes.

If MeiliSearch will not plan to handle that (GitHub handles it for example), I will open an issue to remove the unexpected slash during client declaration in the SDKs, because they all have the same problem 😉
